scope: |
  A smoke CI written in .ssc and run on the v2 native lane: one fast repo-wide suite that
  replaces the heavyweight full CI on the push path (the full suite is preserved as
  scripts/full-ci and stays on schedule/dispatch). Same runner locally and on GitHub.
  WIDENED 2026-07-30: the v2 native lane has NO `exec` native (std/process.ssc declares it;
  int/js/jvm/rust all implement it, v2/runtime/std/os-plugin does not), so a CI runner cannot
  run a subprocess on the lane it is supposed to dogfood. Adding it is a prerequisite, not scope
  creep — without it the runner would have to fall back to the v1 interpreter.
next: teach scripts/ci-status that the per-push verdict is smoke.yml, not ci.yml
